# Never install optional dependencies. Today this excludes:
#   - @google-cloud/firestore / @google-cloud/storage (optional deps of
#     firebase-admin — this app only uses admin.messaging()/admin.credential,
#     never admin.firestore()/admin.storage(), and that pair is the ENTIRE
#     origin of 8 moderate npm-audit findings via their vulnerable transitive
#     uuid/gaxios/google-gax chain). Omitting them removes the vulnerable
#     packages from node_modules entirely instead of just pinning a "fixed"
#     version — `npm audit` reports 0 vulnerabilities with this set.
#   - fsevents / platform-specific native resolver bindings (macOS/arch-only
#     watchers) — harmless to omit; the matching one for this platform would
#     be the only one to install anyway, and by definition an optional
#     dependency's absence must not break its parent package.
# If Firestore/Storage admin features are ever added, remove this line and
# re-run `npm install` — firebase-admin will pull them back in on demand.
#
# GOTCHA (verified empirically): npm's `--omit=<x>` CLI flag REPLACES this
# config value for that invocation instead of merging with it. So a command
# like `npm ci --omit=dev` (no explicit --omit=optional) silently re-installs
# the optional deps this file excludes — this file alone is NOT sufficient
# wherever `--omit=dev` is passed on the command line (Dockerfile, CI). Any
# such command must also pass --omit=optional explicitly. Bare `npm install`
# / `npm ci` / `npm audit` (no --omit flag) read this file correctly on their
# own — it's only an issue when --omit is ALSO given on the CLI.
omit=optional
